// Permit ApproveSale only after the tool has resolved with
// `approved: true`. The `output` field on `context` is optional —
// pre-response requests do not carry one — so we must guard the
// access with `context has output` before reading `context.output.approved`.
// Without that guard, the access is undefined for pre-output requests.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"ApproveSale",
    resource
)
when {
    context has output && context.output.approved == true
};
